# Agent Crew patch 0002: the Claude provider can never skip permissions, and a repo can't grant itself powers.
# - "bypassPermissions" is no longer a valid mode, so creating an agent in it or switching to it is rejected.
# - The SDK is launched with allowDangerouslySkipPermissions: false.
# - providerOptions.extraArgs is never forwarded: raw CLI flags would allow anything, --dangerously-skip-permissions included.
# - Only the user's own Claude settings load, unless the agent is created with providerOptions.trustProjectSettings
#   (Agent Crew sets it only for repos the user has marked trusted). Upstream always loaded the repo's
#   .claude/settings*.json, including its hooks and allow rules.
# Modified by Agent Crew (Apache-2.0 section 4b).

